# Mark AI ideas with (AI)

The owner needs to see which ideas are theirs and which came from an AI assistant, so they can
tell where the project drifts from what they expected.

- In TODO.md, the README and other docs, put **(AI)** before any idea, judgement, priority or
  design choice that came from you. Before an item it marks the whole item; inside an item, the
  part that's yours. Leave the owner's own direction and plain facts about the game unmarked.
- If you're unsure whether the owner asked for something, look for their own words in the past
  chats before treating it as theirs.
- An idea keeps its mark after the owner agrees to it; add that they agreed ("The owner said
  graveyards look neat").
- In chat, when you propose something the owner didn't ask for, say it's your suggestion.

```markdown
<!-- Bad: reads as if the owner wanted it -->
5. **Chimney smoke.** A thin trail of smoke would make the settlements feel lived in.
<!-- Good -->
5. (AI) **Chimney smoke.** A thin trail of smoke would make the settlements feel lived in.
```
